#RingCtrl9 

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#A C-Class Hatchback with Active Cruise Controller (ACC) and blind spot detection is traveling on a road with forward traffic in two lanes and on-coming traffic in a third lane.
#
#The blind spot detection shows alerts for vehicles in the right lane, while the ACC controls the vehicle speed via throttle and brakes. VS Commands are used to model the controllers.  The time gap for the ACC can be modified on the ADAS sensor screen.  The number of bars displayed on the ACC HUD is dependent on the time gap.
#
#The blind spot detection signal includes a low-pass filter that prevents alerts from flashing when on-coming vehicles are detected.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

